From 06145242092a3d67040b3e40c2fab81eebba189a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:31:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] messenger: UART link (KISS port 1) and host-side GGM2 mesh

The radio offers its BK4819 GGM2 modem to a host on the programming UART
(core/messenger/msg_bridge, docs/spec/messenger-link.md): every valid frame
goes to the host with its RSSI, the host's packets are validated and keyed,
and while the host is attached the radio sends no ACK of its own. Silence
for 15 s returns it to standalone behavior.

msg_mesh is the host's side (an ESP32 inside the radio): dedup on
(from, id, type), slotted relays with suppression, ACKs that travel back
over relays, retries. msg_link is the host's encoder/decoder. All portable C
with host tests (make -f boards/rt880/Makefile test-msg).

RT-880: LINK=1 (with MSG=1) builds it in; boards/rt880/link_uart.c is still
an inert stub until the programming-cable USART is traced. Untested on the
radio.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013Y8oYMpHjQAhBgzLpHHNXa
